s in conversations amongst the aged","a":["Natascha Korolija"],"d":"2000-03-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00058-2","pdf":"","k":["Coherence (philosophical gambling strategy)","Situated","Psychology","Conversation","Meaning (existential)","Discourse analysis","Sociology","Communication"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00021-1","t":"Pace Panini: Towards a word-based theory of morphology","a":["Probal Dasgupta"],"d":"2000-03-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00021-1","pdf":"","k":["Pace","Word (group theory)","Psychology","Linguistics","Morphology (biology)","Cognitive science","Philosophy","Geography"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00019-3","t":"La interpretación y la imagen de masas","a":["Jóse Matco Martinez"],"d":"2000-03-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00019-3","pdf":"","k":["Humanities","Psychology","Philosophy"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00055-7","t":"Relating to Ken Kesey's wise man","a":["Varol Akman"],"d":"2000-03-01","abs":"","oa":"green","url":"https://repository.bilkent.edu.tr/bitstreams/349060b0-d32b-4767-aa1c-baff28b664f5/download","pdf":"https://repository.bilkent.edu.tr/bitstreams/349060b0-d32b-4767-aa1c-baff28b664f5/download","k":["Sequence (biology)","Sublime","Philosophy","Linguistics","Epistemology","Art","Aesthetics","Biology"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00053-3","t":"From if to iff: Conditional perfection as pragmatic strengthening","a":["Laurence R. Horn"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"Geis and Zwicky's squib on “conditional perfection” (1971) released a hornet's nest of rebuttal and counter-rebuttal into the pragmatic atmosphere, with many scholars in the area playing alternately the roles of stinger and stingee. Geis and Zwicky's goal was to explain the notorious tendency among introductory logic students and ordinary speakers to ‘perfect’ an if-then conditional of the form of If you mow the lawn, I'll give you five dollars into the corresponding iff biconditional of the form if and only if you mow the lawn, I'll give you five dollars. In an overlapping pair of studies, van der Auwera (1997a,b) has recently contributed a comprehensive survey of the literature on conditional perfection before and since Geis and Zwicky as a microcosm of the development of post-Gricean pragmatic theory. While agreeing with van der Auwera on the centrality of the if → iff move for contemporary pragmatics, I will critique his treatment and offer my own perspective on the data and their ramifications, along with an expanded history that touches on the manifestations of conditional perfection and related inferential fallacies addressed in philosophical treatises, empirical psycholinguistic studies, and self-help primers. By extending the data base to include counterfactuals and other non-predictive conditionals, I will also present problems for Dancygier and Sweetser's (1997) alternative recent account of the CP phenomenon within the mental-spaces framework. The overall focus will be on the implications for the theory of conversational implicature, and in particular of R-based pragmatic strengthening, that can be drawn from the conditions on - and motivation for - conditional perfection.","oa":"hybrid","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0378216699000533/pdf","pdf":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0378216699000533/pdf","k":["Rebuttal","Perfection","Epistemology","Focus (optics)","Psychology","Pragmatics","Social psychology","Linguistics"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00051-x","t":"The semantics of the Japanese imperfective -teiru: An integrative approach","a":["Yasuhiro Shirai"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"This paper attempts to resolve the controversy concerning the conditions under which the Japanese aspectual form -teiru takes different meanings. Kindaichi (1950) and others proposed punctuality of the verb as a trigger for resultative meaning, but Okuda (1978a,b) and Kudo (1995) dismiss the argument that duration is a crucial determinant of the aspectual meaning -teiru takes. This paper proposes that duration is an important factor that determines whether progressive or resultative meaning obtains. It is argued that the previous disagreements between the duration approach (Kindaichi, 1950) and the syntactic approach (Okuda, 1978a,b) can be resolved by taking an integrative approach. It is suggested that the meaning of -teiru is determined in a way that maximally satisfies both types of constraints - temporal and syntactic.","oa":"hybrid","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00051-x","pdf":"","k":["Resultative","Meaning (existential)","Linguistics","Argument (complex analysis)","Semantics (computer science)","Verb","Causative","Duration (music)"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00017-x","t":"Experiencing narrative worlds: On the psychological activities of reading","a":["David S. Miall"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00017-x","pdf":"","k":["Narrative","Reading (process)","Psychology","Psychoanalysis","Sociology","Linguistics","Literature","Art"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00013-2","t":"Pragmatics: Critical concepts","a":["Salvatore Attardo"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00013-2","pdf":"","k":["Pragmatics","Linguistics","Psychology","Sociology","Philosophy"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00073-9","t":"Pragmatics: Critical concepts. Volume II: Speech act theory and particular speech acts","a":["Dorit Bar‐On"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00073-9","pdf":"","k":["Pragmatics","Speech act","Linguistics","Indirect speech","Volume (thermodynamics)","Psychology","Philosophy","Physics"]},{"doi":"10.1016/s0378-2166(99)00077-6","t":"Robert Hopper 1945–1998","a":["Jürgen Streeck"],"d":"2000-02-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s0378-2166(99